<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="H-1992.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>H-1992.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 2197</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>59th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2005 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representatives Clibborn, Moeller and O&apos;Brien</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 02/22/2005.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Finance.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Providing for infrastructure funding.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to infrastructure funding; and creating a new<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>section.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="new"><LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>The legislature recognizes the need to<LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5"/>provide local governments with a new, stable, and broad source of<LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6"/>funding for capital infrastructure.  The legislature recognizes also<LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7"/>the need to adequately fund growth in school districts and the need to<LineNumber line=" 8" page="1,8"/>provide relief to the ongoing affordable housing crisis.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 1	HB 2197</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>